# ORS then SRS (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (w); Dave 2026-10-19: fix now).
# Leg 1, a sound deck: CassWithExitPupil.in, the exit-pupil Return surface (element 5) and the
#   detector (element 6).  The surface's focal length is first set 2.5% long with MODify; ORS
#   recovers the design value (5.5601, pinned to 5 figures), SRS re-slaves the detector to it, and
#   the OPD at the detector is back at the round-off floor (a bound, pin rule 1).
# Leg 2, a starved deck: a COPY of ImageDemo.in with its primary's tenth Zernike coefficient set to
#   5 mm -- the defect the manual's extracted listing carried for a day (a PDF line wrap split
#   '-3.536721061D-05' and the reader took the orphaned '05' as the next term; finding 1.2 (cc),
#   resolved 2026-10-19), which loses 726 of 741 rays before the exit pupil.  ORS used to print
#   'TTL OPD= NaN' there and offer a surface optimized on NaN comparisons; the trial rms now counts
#   only rays that reach the surface, an empty trial is a huge merit, and a start with fewer than
#   three data rays is named and aborted -- the must-fail leg: the pre-fix binary prints the NaN.
# Leg 0, the manual's example (Dave 2026-10-19: an exit pupil is FEX's job; ORS is for a NEAR-FIELD reference
#   surface): CoroExample.in, the first near-field reference surface ret2_1 (element 5, PropType NF1) set 4%
#   long with MODify; ORS recovers the design 6.3293 (5 figures).  Then SRS on the near-field pair (1.2 (gg),
#   Dave: SRS is important): ret2_2 (element 7) disturbed to f 7.0 / z -7.0 and slaved to 5 comes back to
#   f 6.3293 with z NEGATIVE (the diverging end of the through-focus leg: before, the asymmetric-Returns
#   branch wrote the unsigned radius, +6.329, and INT 7 moved 6%); slaving 5 to 7 returns z POSITIVE; a 'no'
#   to the accept prompt leaves the element alone (before, 'no' was accepted: the test was .NE.'n'.OR..NE.'N'),
#   proved by INT 7 reading the design deck's peak after a declined SRS that would have flipped z.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CoroExample.in
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CassWithExitPupil.in
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/ImageDemo.in
old $TMP/CoroExample.in
mod
fElt(5)=6.6
q
ors
5
yes
mod
fElt(7)=7.0
q
mod
zElt(7)=-7.0
q
srs
7
5
yes
srs
5
7
yes
old $TMP/CoroExample.in
srs
7
5
no
int 7
/null
old $TMP/CassWithExitPupil.in
mod
fElt(5)=5.7
q
ors
5
yes
srs
6
5
yes
opd 6
/null
! perl -i -pe 's/-3\.536721061D-05/5d0/' $TMP/ImageDemo.in
old $TMP/ImageDemo.in
ors
12
# EXPECT: fElt\(\s*5\) =\s+6\.600000000D\+00\s+KrElt[\s\S]*?Old f=\s+6\.600000000D\+00\s+New f=\s+6\.3293\d*D\+00
# EXPECT: Old f=\s+7\.000000000D\+00\s+New f=\s+6\.3293\d*D\+00\s+Old z=\s+-7\.000000000D\+00\s+New z=\s+-6\.3293\d*D\+00
# EXPECT: Enter number of element to slave to: \[1\]: 7\s+Reference surface recalculation results:\s+Old f=\s+6\.3293\d*D\+00\s+New f=\s+6\.3293\d*D\+00\s+Old z=\s+6\.3293\d*D\+00\s+New z=\s+6\.3293\d*D\+00
# EXPECT: Accept the new element\? \[YES\]: no[\s\S]*?Peak intensity= 1\.3052\d*D-05
# EXPECT-NOT: New z=\s+6\.329334644D\+00
# EXPECT: fElt\(\s*5\) =\s+5\.700000000D\+00
# EXPECT: Reference surface optimization results:\s+TTL OPD=\s+\d\.\d+D-1\d\s+nCalls=\s+\d+\s+Old f=\s+5\.700000000D\+00\s+New f=\s+5\.5601\d*D\+00
# EXPECT: Enter number of element to slave to: \[1\]: 5\s+Reference surface recalculation results:
# EXPECT: OPD: nPassRays =\s+112,[\s\S]*RMS OPD error is\s+\d\.\d+D-1\d
# EXPECT: ORS: only\s+\d+ of\s+317 test rays reach element\s+11 \(the surface before it\); at least 3 are needed\.\s+ORS: command aborted\.
# EXPECT-NOT: TTL OPD=\s+NaN
# EXPECT-NOT: New f=\s+\d\.\d+D\+41
# EXPECT-NOT: Debug: VAR_NAM
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
